<?ish ishref="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9" version="1" lang="en-US"?><task id="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title id="GUID-610723A5-45E0-431A-BEBF-3D9C48811266">Improve Print Quality</title> 
  <shortdesc>If the quality of your printed documents does not meet your expectations, there are common causes to address. 
  </shortdesc> 
  <prolog> 
	 <metadata> 
		<keywords> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="MODEL=810AIO">810AIO</keyword> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="MODEL=820AIO">820AIO</keyword> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="MODEL=910AIO">910AIO</keyword> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="MODEL=920AIO">920AIO</keyword> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="Series='800_Series'"> 800 Series</keyword> 
		  <keyword ishcondition="Series='900_Series'"> 900 Series</keyword> 
		  <keyword>Acadian</keyword> 
		  <indexterm>printing<indexterm>improving quality</indexterm></indexterm> 
		  <indexterm>quality<indexterm>improving print</indexterm></indexterm> 
		</keywords> </metadata>
  </prolog> 
  <taskbody> 
	 <context id="GUID-6D3E3495-C23F-4D51-806C-D7C153676BCC"> 
		<p>Common causes of poor print quality are: 
		<ul id="UL_8BE7C93541294E8F95362CD56B196898"> 
		  <li id="LI_A96CDE2139014E16B98AF55F7E21AFC6">Paper loaded improperly. 
		  </li> 
		  <li id="LI_8134520907C840369CC191853379D4D2">Paper type needs to be appropriate for document type. 
		  </li> 
		  <li id="LI_9EC29F3BFCD24BC0A33FE4C870815983">Print quality setting is too low for the type of document. 
		  </li> 
		  <li id="LI_286B3B485AF1466297C4A31D5F3DEC21">Ink cartridges are low or empty. 
		  </li> 
		</ul> 
		</p> 
	 </context> 
	 <steps id="GUID-45D61AA0-E06B-4191-8977-0B830BA1BC16"> 
		<step id="STEP_EE1552D3E5CA47FB838DED98E5483D00"> 
		  <cmd>Identify the specific issues with the print quality. 
		  </cmd> 
		  <choices id="CHOICES_B8E35BE8E1E3476EBD4905812BFC41E0"> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_B5C9F69F5A7745E5B2AEDD1DEE5A8824">If the colors are wrong, then go to 
				<xref href="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9#GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9/STEP_7E07B92F803E4EB88032CA1E9B57F902">step 2</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_5C95F4CF61004DBE9268C2CC496D3A2D">If the print output is fuzzy or blurry, then go to 
				<xref href="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9#GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9/STEP_B75FA4E7A744406B9101C8BDF615321B">step 3</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
		  </choices> 
		</step> 
		<step id="STEP_7E07B92F803E4EB88032CA1E9B57F902"> 
		  <cmd> 
			 <ph conref="GUID-34DEA6CD-2AFB-4E02-862B-BCA31196E12A#GUID-34DEA6CD-2AFB-4E02-862B-BCA31196E12A/ERR_EMPTY_INK">Is 
				<xref href="GUID-09DF91A0-61EE-4E24-B3E9-EC6996F17470"> 
				  <msgnum conref="GUID-09DF91A0-61EE-4E24-B3E9-EC6996F17470#GUID-09DF91A0-61EE-4E24-B3E9-EC6996F17470/ERROR_206">Error Code 206</msgnum> 
				</xref> displayed on the LCD or are any of the ink cartridges empty? 
			 </ph> 
		  </cmd> 
		  <choices id="CHOICES_F95C4FEA2333489AAFD8A45ED9AFF172"> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_851B6577AE104B9690D214C06746BB77">If Yes, then 
				<xref href="GUID-B191D266-062D-4FBA-9A78-736652EA94A0#GUID-B191D266-062D-4FBA-9A78-736652EA94A0">replace the empty ink cartridge</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_62AC5F04E09E4E15ACBD393144846DE6">In No, then go to 
				<xref href="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9#GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9/STEP_B75FA4E7A744406B9101C8BDF615321B">step 3</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
		  </choices> 
		</step> 
		<step id="STEP_B75FA4E7A744406B9101C8BDF615321B"> 
		  <cmd>Is the paper loaded with the right or print side down? 
		  </cmd> 
		  <info> 
			 <ph conref="GUID-57E71C4B-56B4-41B2-B07A-B15B61CE110D#GUID-57E71C4B-56B4-41B2-B07A-B15B61CE110D/PH_RIGHT_SIDE_DOWN">For papers that have a right side and a wrong side, such as photo paper, you must load the right or print side down in the paper tray.</ph> 
		  </info> 
		  <choices id="CHOICES_505A12DB64484F79B91BBFAC73FF0D1E"> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_F0D4DCC52D8F49B6897406C37FFFBCC7">If Yes, then go to the 
				<xref href="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9#GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9/STEP_10061D48A46242D2BC60A65E9A4016E6">next step</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_918FD358FA7D4CBA9D6984A962ED44BF">In No, place the paper in the tray with the print side down. 
			 </choice> 
		  </choices> 
		</step> 
		<step id="STEP_10061D48A46242D2BC60A65E9A4016E6"> 
		  <cmd>If you are printing a photograph or an illustration, do you have proper paper in the paper tray? 
		  </cmd> 
		  <choices id="CHOICES_B0A7558035744D389653C64AB5846DF8"> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_8E2B492F28FD4A81A637E0C41E15F57F">If Yes, then go to the 
				<xref href="GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9#GUID-8BBCB12E-75F4-45D6-B209-DB3F3FDAE8A9/STEP_63C7A93A51754DCCB97214EEC93C09BB">next step</xref>. 
			 </choice> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_4891DF31ED394C6288202D271A6D94C8">If No, place the appropriate paper in the tray right side down. 
			 </choice> 
		  </choices> 
		  <stepxmp>For example, if you want to print a photograph with good quality, you must use photo paper. 
		  </stepxmp> 
		</step> 
		<step id="STEP_63C7A93A51754DCCB97214EEC93C09BB"> 
		  <cmd>Is the print quality set to High? 
		  </cmd> 
		  <info>When you print a document from the computer, the document application allows you to specify the settings, including the quality, for the printer. 
		  </info> 
		  <choices id="CHOICES_9B87ABEAB1534AB28BA573C19EE2F9C2"> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_A0E1617C361143ADBF528D37B4E8DDC3">In Yes, then go to the 
				<ph varref="company_name_short">Acadian, Inc.</ph> web site(<ph ishcondition="Region=NA"> 
				  <xref conref="GUID-F350E035-AB00-49FB-AD74-C1DE90681530#GUID-F350E035-AB00-49FB-AD74-C1DE90681530/US_URL"></xref> 
				</ph><ph ishcondition="Region in (EU,PR)"> 
				  <xref conref="GUID-F350E035-AB00-49FB-AD74-C1DE90681530#GUID-F350E035-AB00-49FB-AD74-C1DE90681530/GERMAN_URL"></xref> 
				</ph>. 
			 </choice> 
			 <choice id="CHOICE_2664EEC38A034002868F6B403BFAD392">If No, then you need to change the print quality setting. 
			 </choice> 
		  </choices> 
		</step> 
	 </steps> 
  </taskbody> 
</task>
